<% content_for :title, "Hack Club NDA API Docs" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "docs-page" %>

<section class="docs-shell">
  <article class="docs-content">
    <section class="docs-section">
      <div class="endpoint-heading">
        <span class="http-method">GET</span>
        <code>/api/v1/nda_status/:slack_id</code>
      </div>
      <p>Replace <code>:slack_id</code> with a Slack member ID. Note that this endpoint is public and does not require authentication. Do not file security reports against this endpoint claiming it leaks private information.</p>

      <h2>Request</h2>
      <pre><code>curl <%= api_v1_nda_status_url(slack_id: "U0123ABCDEF") %></code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <h2>Successful response</h2>
      <p>A known member with a signature for the current NDA receives <code>signed</code> and a signing timestamp.</p>
      <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slack_id": "U0123ABCDEF",
  "status": "signed",
  "nda_version": "<%= NdaDocument::VERSION %>",
  "signed_at": "2025-04-02T15:04:05Z"
}</code></pre>

      <p>An unknown member, or a member without a signature for the current version, receives <code>not_signed</code>. In that case, <code>signed_at</code> is omitted.</p>
      <pre><code>{
  "slack_id": "U0123ABCDEF",
  "status": "not_signed",
  "nda_version": "<%= NdaDocument::VERSION %>"
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <h2>Invalid Slack ID</h2>
      <p>Unknown or malformed IDs receive a <code>400 Bad Request</code>.</p>
      <pre><code>{
  "error": "invalid_slack_id"
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <h2>Rate limit</h2>
      <p>Each client IP may make up to 10 requests per second across the site. Additional requests receive <code>429 Too Many Requests</code> with a <code>Retry-After</code> header.</p>
      <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: text/plain
Retry-After: 1

Retry later</code></pre>
    </section>
  </article>
</section>
